hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2593","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) forbade Muhakla and Muzabnah. \n Imam al-Darmi (may God have mercy on him) said: They ask to sell the crops standing in the fields in exchange for wheat. Ibn al-Musayyib also said the same."
"2594","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (PBUH) permitted the sale of ``Araya'' in exchange for wet or dry dates and did not permit any other (form)."
"2595","On the authority of Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever buys any kind of grain"," should not sell it before taking possession of it.\"""""
"2596","Amr ibn Shuaib narrated from his father, he from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade two conditions in a loan and a sale and a sale, and taking advantage of something before taking possession of it."
"2597","Salim narrated on the authority of his father Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever buys a slave and does not make a bet on his property"," then for him there is nothing of the property of the slave.\"""""
"2598","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade two types of beyah and two types of clothing, and munabzah and malamazah. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The sale is that the seller throws (cloth, etc.) towards Jupiter and Jupiter throws (clothes etc.) towards the seller, (and this ends the sale)."
"2599","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of deceit and the sale of pebbles. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: Baya al-Hassa is that when a pebble is thrown, the baya will be completed."
"2600","Sayyidna Samura bin Jundab (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of an animal on loan for an animal. Then Hasan, may Allah have mercy on him, forgot this hadith. And Ja'far, may God have mercy on him, did not say that Hasan, may God have mercy on him, forgot this hadith."
"2601","The freed slave of the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, borrowed a young camel, so when the charity camels came, Sayyiduna Abu Rafi, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I was ordered by the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, to return this man's camel. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Give him the best four-quarter camel. Better are those who pay their debts well.\"" \n Imam al-Darmi (may Allah have mercy on him) said: This hadith supports his view that it is permissible to sell an animal in exchange for an animal."""
"2602","Sayyidina Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Do not go ahead and meet those who bring grain to the city from outside"," and whoever goes and meets this (caravan) and buys some goods from him"," then the owner of the seller has the option (whether to keep the deal or cancel it) after reaching the market.\"""""
"2603","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \None of you should interfere in the buying and selling of anyone"," and do not meet the caravans until they reach the market"," and do not raise the price if you do not intend to buy.\"""""
"2604","Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud Ansari (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the price of a dog, the wages and earnings of a wicked and adulterous woman, and the sweets of a priest. \n Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: The sweetness of a priest is the reward that he gets by telling the things of the unseen."
"2605","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: When the verse \Sud\"" was revealed at the end of Surah Al-Baqarah"," the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) went outside and recited it to the Companions (may Allah be pleased with him). Then prohibited the trade of alcohol."""
"2606","The previous example is mentioned in this document as well. The translation has passed on O."
"2607","Abd al-Rahman bin Wa'ala said: I asked Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, about the skin of a dead body, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \By tanning it"," it becomes pure.\"" When he offered a musk"," the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: \""O Abu So-and-so! Don't you know that Allah has forbidden alcohol?\"" He said: No"," by Allah"," I do not know. He said: \""So listen"," Allah has forbidden it (alcohol).\"" So the man turned to his servant and said to him: Go"," take it to Hazura (name of the place) and sell it. The Messenger of Allah"," may God bless him and grant him peace"," said: \""O Abu So-and-so! Don't you know that the Holy One who made it forbidden to drink it has also made it forbidden to sell it.\"" The narrator said: So he ordered and the wine was poured into the field."""
"2608","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) said: The Messenger of Allah (SAW) forbade the sale of Wala and its habah. Imam al-Darmi, may God have mercy on him, said: It is a practice that a villa cannot be sold or bequeathed."
